  "strategy": "### 1. Approach and Rationale\n\nOur approach combines adaptive gradient descent with an iterative cutting-plane method to systematically explore and exploit the problem's structure. The key innovation is dynamically adjusting the search strategy based on the optimization landscape:\n\n1. **Two-Phase Optimization**:\n   - **Initial Exploration**: Use a continuation method starting from a uniform sample distribution.\n   - **Exploitation**: Switch to a cutting-plane approach once an initial minimum is found.\n\n2. **Cutting-Plane Method**:\n   - Linearize the non-convex bilinear terms at each iteration.\n   - Solve a sequence of convex relaxations to tighten the bound.\n\n3. **Dynamic Adjustment**:\n   - Start with a coarse discretization.\n   - Refine the resolution near promising regions based on gradient information.\n\n### 2. Mathematical Specification\n\nWe represent h as a step function with n_points discretization points. Let dx = 2.0 / n_points. Define the overlap integral:\n\nC\u2085 = max\u2096 \u2211\u2090 h[a](1 - h[a + k]) dx\n\nSubject to:\n0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1\n\u2211 h[i] = n_points / 2\n\nThe bilinear terms h[a](1 - h[a + k]) are convexified iteratively.\n\n### 3. Implementation Procedure\n\n#### Initialization\n1. Set n_points = 100, dx = 2.0 / 100.\n2. If initial_h_values exists:\n   a. Interpolate to n_points discretization.\n   b. Normalize to meet sum constraint.\n3. Else:\n   a. Initialize h as uniform.\n\n#### Optimization Loop\n1. For i in 0 to max_iterations:\n   a. Compute current overlap integral C\u2085.\n   b. If improvement detected, refine grid around active regions.\n   c. Formulate convex relaxation with current linearization.\n   d. Solve with CVXPY.\n   e. Update h using solution.\n   f. Clip and rescale.\n\n#### Grid Refinement\n1. Compute gradient magnitude across h.\n2. Refine regions with high gradient variation.\n3. Interpolate solution to new grid.\n\n### 4. Search Choices and Variations\n\n1. **Initial Resolution**: 100 points for efficiency.\n2. **Refinement Threshold**: Top 20% gradients.\n3. **Solver Settings**: CBC with standard tolerances.\n4. **Dynamic Budget**: Allocate 70% to convex solves, 30% to exploration.\n\n### 5. Compute Budget and Robustness\n\n1. **Time Estimate**: ~500 seconds for full iterations.\n2. **Robustness**:\n   - Maintain best solution at every iteration.\n   - Heuristic refinement prevents overfitting to local minima.\n   - Automatic restart after 100 iterations without improvement.\n\n### 6. Validation and Return Contract\n\n1. Ensure h satisfies constraints:\n   - 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1\n   - \u2211h[i] = n_points / 2\n2. Re-evaluate C\u2085 using evaluator to validate.\n3. Return best found h and C\u2085.",
